WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Through Misa-san's magic,

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.620
I stand here, six years
in the past.

00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:08.800
Here, I met a six-years-smaller Yumiko-chan.

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:12.770
And this bad mage came
here, I guess...

00:00:12.770 --> 00:00:15.720
It was the first real magic
I've ever seen.

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:19.750
I turned my back on my
normal, everyday life

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:21.450
and stepped into a very
dangerous world.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.130
I'd be lying if I said
I wasn't scared.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:26.580
But I don't regret it.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.000
After all, I met
Yumiko-chan here.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.000
After all, I met
Koyomi here.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:05.140
The nice town that
the kitty lives in

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:09.290
is a fun, fun town of cats.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:10.480
6 Years Ago

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:10.480
December 24th

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:16.700
Let's all dance with everyone,
every night!

00:02:20.270 --> 00:02:21.210
It smells good.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:24.750
Well, then.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:27.680
Your name's Morishita
Koyomi-chan, right?

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.160
You said you're here to see me,

00:02:30.160 --> 00:02:31.530
but this is the first time
we've met, right?

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:32.480
Y-Yes.

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.700
I meet you much further
in the future.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:38.350
I came here from six
years from now.

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.500
That's an interesting story
you have there.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.500
So, you're a time traveler?

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:44.160
What about that silver-haired
girl with you?

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.990
Yumiko-chan isn't...

00:02:47.820 --> 00:02:49.090
Yumiko-chan...

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:57.170
Oh? Three people with
impressive Codes.

00:02:57.850 --> 00:03:00.160
I'm definitely outnumbered now.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:04.550
I'll settle my debt with you another
time, Anehara Misa.

00:03:04.550 --> 00:03:06.850
I'm trying to tell you, I'm not her!

00:03:06.850 --> 00:03:07.670
Who are you?

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:09.470
I have no business with you.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:12.690
Oh, but I thought you had a little
something with Anehara Misa?

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:15.940
You're quite lucky,
mademoiselle.

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.680
I'll be looking forward to
the next time we meet.

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:25.460
I wonder if Yumiko-chan's okay.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.290
I can feel it.

00:03:38.290 --> 00:03:40.330
The Code which woke
me from my sleep,

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:41.980
the one constructed
by machines.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:45.530
A new, but nostalgic, sensation.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.240
I remember it-the Code of my
arch-enemy, Anehara Kenjuro.

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.410
Prepare yourself!

00:04:00.370 --> 00:04:02.630
Bastard!

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:06.770
Fate is cleverly crafted.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:10.690
Once, I fought both Cristbarth
and Kenjuro,

00:04:10.690 --> 00:04:14.580
and now, I have met their
descendants here.

00:04:18.710 --> 00:04:21.840
I-I guess this body won't last long.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.180
I must hurry and obtain
the Sorceress's Library.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.830
What is this?

00:04:39.390 --> 00:04:40.600
Be careful.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:42.660
There are PCB's inside.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.230
Not only in that tree stump.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:47.410
The toilet bowl there and
that old clock...

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:49.410
They all have computers inside.

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.410
Why are there computers in-

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:54.260
Well, it's not like I don't get it.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:01.460
A-A-A ghost!

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.560
I can't see anything.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:07.670
Really?

00:05:07.670 --> 00:05:08.570
Yeah.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:12.280
Calm down. That's a ghostscript.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:12.970
Huh?

00:05:13.390 --> 00:05:17.440
When a strong image is burned
into something as Code...

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.810
That's a ghostscript.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:25.120
S-So, they're not ghosts?

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:26.910
When living things die,

00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:32.190
a lot of them leave particularly strong Codes
behind. So they're called ghostscripts.

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:34.400
But they don't require someone
or something to die.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:35.650
That's good.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:38.960
Oh, a cat.

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:41.340
And as usual, I can't see it.

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:48.010
So, the cat just now
was a ghostscript?

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:50.660
But because it looks like a cat,

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.660
doesn't that mean
it has to be a cat?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.420
It's just a cat!

00:05:55.030 --> 00:05:58.890
As I imagined, I cannot help
you regarding this matter.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:02.580
I don't like cats or crime.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:11.030
So the reason you've
come to the past

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:12.740
hasn't yet been clarified?

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.720
I'm sorry.

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:18.930
If I don't convey what happened in
order, I can't explain it very well.

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:20.970
So, what happens?

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:22.140
Oh, yeah!

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:26.630
This is a problem... I thought
I'd ask Yumiko,

00:06:26.630 --> 00:06:28.630
but I guess she has some
cat-inflicted trauma.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.330
Did something happen between
that cat and Yumiko-chan?

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.780
A long time ago.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:37.840
Yumiko was still a child, and no one could
have stopped what was coming.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.370
You've known Yumiko-chan that long?

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.400
That was the first time I met her,

00:06:44.400 --> 00:06:46.900
six years ago on Christmas Eve.

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.800
What were you going to
ask Ichinose to do?

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:53.030
I was going to ask her to take
a peek into the past.

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:54.710
The past?

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.920
Oh, Koyomi! Could I ask
you to do something?

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.460
The password?

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:05.180
Yeah. The ghostscripts here

00:07:05.180 --> 00:07:08.030
are all Codes I made
a long time ago.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.840
It looks like the Christmas Shopper
is the problem here.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.980
Christmas Shopper?

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:15.480
So, to figure out what's happening,

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:18.340
we'll have to go back six years, to
when the code was executed.

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:21.320
I want you to have a look at
its administrator password.

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:22.080
I see.

00:07:22.320 --> 00:07:24.710
You don't remember
the password?

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:28.000
Well, given that it was a crime,

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.900
I must have destroyed the
evidence in my head, too.

00:07:30.900 --> 00:07:35.170
But how will you look six
years into the past?

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.680
That's what the goggles are for.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:42.020
We'll run the Codes accumulated in
objects and locations in reverse

00:07:42.020 --> 00:07:44.440
to reconstruct visuals of the past.

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:48.000
You could call it a practical
application of ghostscript.

00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:50.680
Anyway, thanks, Koyomi.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:51.780
Good luck, Morishita.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.140
W-Wait! Um, I don't think
I'm ready for this!

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.290
And that's what happened.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:09.650
I see...

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:12.250
So how do you plan
on getting back?

00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.340
I'm sorry. I didn't ask.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:20.040
You know that you might be unable
to return to your normal world?

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.050
What?!

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.050
B-But...

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:26.350
How long has it been since
you came to this world?

00:08:26.350 --> 00:08:31.230
Uh, probably about two hours?

00:08:31.230 --> 00:08:35.660
You think I'd leave a girl there,
wearing goggles for two hours?

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.960
This is just a guess,

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:43.700
but maybe you're extremely
sensitive to ghostscripts.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:48.200
And the data from this world reaches your
brain having been greatly compressed.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:52.830
That's why, in the world six years from
now, not much time has passed.

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:54.650
So what should I do?

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:55.750
I dunno.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:56.510
No way-

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:59.530
Hey, you're having gyoza
on Christmas?

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:01.880
Who cares? It's good.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.690
Anyway, what's that about?

00:09:03.690 --> 00:09:05.810
This wash basin is yours, isn't it?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:06.730
Do something about it!

00:09:06.730 --> 00:09:08.780
I'm sorry!

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:12.140
Did you summon that wash basin?

00:09:12.140 --> 00:09:13.070
Yes.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:22.710
Something with this much mass?

00:09:23.180 --> 00:09:26.590
Summoning magic is really
difficult, you know!

00:09:26.590 --> 00:09:30.370
In exchange, I can't use
any other magic.

00:09:31.030 --> 00:09:34.720
No matter what I try, the Code
changes into a wash basin.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.880
How large a Code are we talking?

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:39.380
If it's just me and one Code,
it doesn't matter how big...

00:09:39.380 --> 00:09:41.680
That's really impressive!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.980
Really?

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:47.000
Sis, good grown-ups don't take everything
a kid says seriously.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.170
Shut up!

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.380
We might be able
to do something.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:54.980
If everything you say is true,

00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:57.730
we might be able to return
you to your own world.

00:09:57.730 --> 00:09:58.900
Really?

00:09:59.270 --> 00:10:01.760
If we were to execute
a large-scale

00:10:01.760 --> 00:10:04.860
magical activation Code that
affected all of this world,

00:10:04.930 --> 00:10:08.700
it'd be the same as you executing
real-world Code,

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:12.430
since you're deeply intertwined
with this one.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.000
By turning it into a wash basin,

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.420
we might be able to stop the
ghostscript from running.

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.530
H-How do we do that?

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.400
You're right on time.

00:10:22.400 --> 00:10:26.940
I just started setting up some large-scale
magic that uses a network.

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:30.750
That's the Christmas Shopper.
You've heard of it, haven't you?

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:31.940
Y-Yeah!

00:10:47.870 --> 00:10:49.440
You saw that, didn't you?

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.080
Jeez...

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.410
Father!

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:04.220
Mother!

00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.830
You're trying to make
me feel better?

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:16.180
It's okay. I'm not lonely at all.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.230
Nine o'clock.

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.210
You have until nine tonight,

00:11:27.210 --> 00:11:29.970
when I finish my adjustments
to the Christmas Shopper.

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:31.990
So if you want to save
Yumiko-chan,

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:33.660
you'll have until then.

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.870
I will warn you about
one thing, though.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:41.990
You may only be looking at this
world through a ghostscript,

00:11:41.990 --> 00:11:43.180
but don't let your guard down.

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:44.130
Huh?

00:11:44.130 --> 00:11:47.660
You're extremely tangled
in this Code,

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:49.850
so if you get hurt in this world,

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:53.760
there's a chance it could
affect your future self.

00:11:53.760 --> 00:11:55.690
What does that mean?

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:58.040
If you die in this world,

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.930
your self six years from
now could die, too!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:08.180
Sitting here until it's time might
be your safest option, but...

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:10.310
What will you do?
Will you still go?

00:12:13.340 --> 00:12:14.470
Yes!

00:12:14.980 --> 00:12:16.640
Yumiko-chan's young,

00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:19.840
but she's facing all this by herself!
I can't leave her alone!

00:12:23.360 --> 00:12:24.640
You okay?

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.760
Don't fall when there
isn't anything there.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:28.540
O-Ow...

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:32.110
Here, I'll give you this.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:35.060
I'm fine. I have some band-aids.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.040
You fall a lot, don't you?

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:38.740
Take it.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:40.550
O-Ow...

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:41.470
It's not like you can
have too many.

00:12:41.470 --> 00:12:42.420
Thanks.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:45.280
Come on, let's go.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:47.260
We're searching for
Yumiko, right?

00:12:47.260 --> 00:12:48.060
Yeah!

00:12:54.330 --> 00:12:56.020
Are you looking for someone?

00:12:56.020 --> 00:12:56.780
Yumiko-chan!

00:12:57.270 --> 00:12:59.000
Hey, Katamari!

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.770
Did you want something
from me?

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:07.300
Almost there.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:10.810
If I activate the Code in
the Christmas Shopper,

00:13:10.810 --> 00:13:13.770
though it's nothing more
than a bunch of silicon,

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:18.040
it'll become an unstoppable amulet embedded
with 2048 variable Codes.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.760
But to think the Code
I constructed

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:26.230
still has an effect six
years from now...

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:30.750
I wonder who it is.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.380
Who is it?

00:13:33.380 --> 00:13:36.260
If you're trying to sell me a newspaper,
I already have one.

00:13:36.610 --> 00:13:39.140
Joyeux Noël, mademoiselle.

00:13:39.140 --> 00:13:41.240
Could you bring me
Anehara Misa?

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:44.420
No one's here but me,

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.570
and I don't think Anehara Misa
has any business with you.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:48.900
Who are you?

00:13:48.900 --> 00:13:51.270
Who am I? I'm a good Santa!

00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:54.120
And who are you?
An evil skeleton?

00:13:57.320 --> 00:14:00.590
I am Jean-Jacques Guibarthez.

00:14:00.590 --> 00:14:02.520
I've heard of him.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:05.790
Some mage who lived around
one hundred years ago, right?

00:14:05.790 --> 00:14:07.610
You don't have to believe me.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:12.240
I'm here for the Sorceress's Library
left behind by Digitalis.

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.660
Digitalis, the legendary sorceress.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.150
Digitalis Flammalacia,

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:25.700
the great, vile mage said to have long ago taken
the lives of more than 100,000 men in Europe.

00:14:25.700 --> 00:14:30.670
She was said to have returned to life countless times to
go on rampages, even after being burned to death.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:38.430
I've heard rumors as to the location of Digitalis's
library, which holds the secret to her revival.

00:14:38.430 --> 00:14:41.230
The Sorceress's Library
does exist.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:44.860
It should be sealed within
the staff, Kerykeion.

00:14:44.860 --> 00:14:46.110
I see.

00:14:46.110 --> 00:14:49.150
So what do you need here?

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:53.240
I was thinking of having Anehara Misa
recuse herself from this matter.

00:14:53.240 --> 00:14:54.700
That sure sounds selfish.

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:56.500
In exchange,

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:58.740
I won't get in the way
of the large-scale

00:14:58.740 --> 00:15:01.230
magical ceremony that
Anehara Misa is performing.

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:03.030
It's a fair trade, don't you think?

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:07.710
I, not the Anehara Misa you're looking for,
am performing the magical ceremony.

00:15:08.240 --> 00:15:14.120
Oh, I thought it was a magic done
by Anehara's descendants,

00:15:14.120 --> 00:15:15.950
but I guess it was you, after all.

00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:20.220
I have no interest in the Sorceress's
Library or Kerykeion.

00:15:20.220 --> 00:15:23.490
But if it bothers you, I'll
make a promise to you.

00:15:24.030 --> 00:15:24.990
Really?

00:15:24.990 --> 00:15:28.260
How does this sound? We won't
get in each other's way

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:30.520
until either one of us finishes
what we're doing.

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:33.470
So, the early bird can get
in the other's way?

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:40.400
That's not really a promise,
but more the way it is.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:41.690
Sounds good.

00:15:41.690 --> 00:15:44.730
Let's see each other again,
should chance so provide.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.250
Be careful.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:04.760
She might look like a kid, but you
always have to be prepared.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:09.010
Hey! You've been staring
at me for a while now!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.700
Don't get mad.

00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:14.610
I won't!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:17.210
I'd be more offended if you
were hiding something!

00:16:17.210 --> 00:16:18.580
Now, what is it?

00:16:18.980 --> 00:16:22.740
Uh, um... Um... You
won't get mad?

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:23.940
I will!

00:16:26.380 --> 00:16:27.910
U-Um...

00:16:29.320 --> 00:16:35.360
I-I was just thinking that those breasts of
yours, which look like the Siberian plains,

00:16:35.360 --> 00:16:39.100
will grow to resemble Mount
Everest in a few years!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:40.190
What?!

00:16:40.190 --> 00:16:42.710
I was just thinking about
how nice that is!

00:16:42.710 --> 00:16:45.450
But right now, mine are
bigger than yours!

00:16:45.450 --> 00:16:47.140
What are you saying?!

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.990
I'm still in grade school!

00:16:48.990 --> 00:16:50.820
Stop making fun of me!

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:54.040
Transform to swords, my Code!

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:58.740
I won't let you
get away!

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.740
Yumiko-chan!

00:16:58.740 --> 00:17:01.010
Stop, Yumiko-chan!

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:08.500
Are you okay? Sorry.

00:17:08.500 --> 00:17:11.890
That was my loss, Anehara Misa!

00:17:11.890 --> 00:17:13.780
Huh? Anehara?

00:17:13.780 --> 00:17:15.670
I'm talking about you!

00:17:15.670 --> 00:17:17.940
I'm not Misa-san.

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:18.510
Huh?

00:17:18.510 --> 00:17:20.710
I'm Morishita Koyomi.

00:17:20.710 --> 00:17:22.440
I've come here from six
years in the future.

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:26.030
I'm Misa-san's student, and I'm
also a high-school student.

00:17:26.030 --> 00:17:28.490
You've got to be kidding me!

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:29.490
Why's that?

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:32.450
It's impossible for you to
be from the future.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:33.520
There!

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:35.790
Hey, w-wait a second!

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:48.290
How about some food?

00:17:48.890 --> 00:17:51.540
I'm busy right now,
so go on ahead.

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:54.350
Right. Don't push yourself
too hard.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.760
If I'm going to fight
with Guibarthez,

00:17:56.760 --> 00:17:58.430
I'll need my I's dotted
and my T's crossed.

00:17:58.860 --> 00:18:00.250
I need to hurry.

00:18:03.430 --> 00:18:07.770
Basically, you're like an
alien to this world.

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.100
Alien?

00:18:09.900 --> 00:18:12.360
You are a high-school
student, right?

00:18:12.360 --> 00:18:15.200
Y-Yeah, but...

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:18.650
Then you should at least know
"alien" can be used that way.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:20.460
I'm sorry...

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:21.620
Jeez.

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:27.360
Are you hungry, Yumiko-chan?

00:18:28.040 --> 00:18:29.540
I'm fine!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.630
Wait just a second!

00:18:30.630 --> 00:18:31.940
H-Hey...

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:34.010
I'm going to buy a hamburger
over there.

00:18:34.010 --> 00:18:35.620
I'm hungry, too!

00:18:42.730 --> 00:18:44.980
Mind if I sit next to you?

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:45.630
Huh?

00:18:50.010 --> 00:18:54.460
Do you know the story of "The President
and The Elephant," little lady?

00:18:54.460 --> 00:18:57.210
Huh? What are you even saying?

00:18:57.210 --> 00:19:00.900
It's about which is stronger, the
president or the elephant.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.090
Among all living creatures, the elephant
is the strongest animal on land.

00:19:04.090 --> 00:19:08.840
But a hunter with a gun can
easily take out an elephant.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:12.920
But if that hunter fights with
his wife, he'll lose to her.

00:19:13.270 --> 00:19:14.600
And?

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:16.610
If you try to find the
strongest person,

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:20.260
you'll eventually end up with the
President of the United States.

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:23.710
He's the strongest because he commands
the strongest military.

00:19:23.710 --> 00:19:25.880
What are you actually
trying to say?

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:31.710
But if you locked the president and an elephant
in the Oval Office, what would happen?

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:34.860
An elephant and a human?
That wouldn't even be a fight!

00:19:35.410 --> 00:19:41.560
The elephant would definitely win.
So which does that make the strongest?

00:19:41.980 --> 00:19:44.780
I don't know. What's the answer?

00:19:45.560 --> 00:19:49.350
The answer depends
on how one thinks.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:54.090
Little girl, which do you think you
are, an elephant or a hunter?

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.580
I might be the president.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:58.330
You shouldn't lie.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:02.030
You shouldn't talk to someone
you just met like that!

00:20:02.820 --> 00:20:05.640
Is that staff so important to you?

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:09.790
Why are you so worried?

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:12.260
This staff is important to me.

00:20:12.260 --> 00:20:14.370
I won't give it to anyone!

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:19.270
I think that staff will only
be important to you

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:23.440
after you carve your
own history into it.

00:20:23.440 --> 00:20:25.270
Mind your own business!

00:20:25.270 --> 00:20:30.060
The curse placed on your life
is my greatest gift to you.

00:20:30.060 --> 00:20:31.280
What?

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.920
Treasure it well.

00:20:32.920 --> 00:20:33.820
What is going-

00:20:33.820 --> 00:20:38.060
You mustn't hand Kerykeion
over to Guibarthez.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:39.970
If necessary...

00:20:56.180 --> 00:20:58.060
I bought some!

00:21:00.200 --> 00:21:02.550
Here's yours, Yumiko-chan.

00:21:02.810 --> 00:21:04.850
Oh, don't worry about paying me.

00:21:04.850 --> 00:21:07.350
I might be small, but
I'm older than you!

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.720
Where is the knife and fork?

00:21:13.720 --> 00:21:14.370
Huh?

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:17.210
There isn't a knife and fork!

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:21.760
How do you use a knife?

00:21:22.960 --> 00:21:24.740
Wh-What?

00:21:24.740 --> 00:21:27.750
Did I say something strange?

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:32.090
Yumiko-chan, you eat a
hamburger like this.

00:21:38.570 --> 00:21:39.250
See?

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:47.600
It's good.

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:48.260
Isn't it?

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:56.600
Food tastes better when you're
eating with someone else!

00:21:56.600 --> 00:21:57.390
What's wrong?

00:21:58.230 --> 00:22:00.290
N-Nothing at all!

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:05.320
Huh? Yumiko-chan?

00:22:09.900 --> 00:22:13.510
Bonsoir, mademoiselle.

00:23:46.370 --> 00:23:50.690
The silver-haired girl's staff, Kerykeion,
is taken away, with nothing she can do.

00:23:50.690 --> 00:23:53.530
While the time limit,
9 PM, approaches,

00:23:53.530 --> 00:23:56.360
Morishita Koyomi runs through
the streets of Ginza,

00:23:56.360 --> 00:23:58.730
so she can save a friend.

00:24:03.710 --> 00:24:06.960
Lesson 5:   Assigned Reading

00:24:07.590 --> 00:24:10.760
Hi! Morishita Koyomi here.

00:24:10.760 --> 00:24:14.770
It's hopelessly hot...
Anehara Misa here.

00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:17.960
What are we learning
about this time?

00:24:17.960 --> 00:24:21.290
Koyomi, what do you think of
when I say summer vacation?

00:24:21.290 --> 00:24:24.330
Hm... The beach!

00:24:24.330 --> 00:24:28.550
Bzzt! You should have
thought of homework.

00:24:28.550 --> 00:24:30.440
Assigned reading, too.

00:24:30.440 --> 00:24:32.190
Wh-Why?

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:39.140
And here's the homework for you, the audience
that watches Koyomi and me.

00:24:39.140 --> 00:24:43.340
Teacher, this is obviously going
to be some sort of promotion!

00:24:43.340 --> 00:24:45.660
Don't worry about it.
Don't worry about it.

00:24:45.660 --> 00:24:53.000
Your assigned reading is obviously Sakurazaka Hiroshi-san's
<i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou!</i>

00:24:53.020 --> 00:24:58.010
<i>Yoku Wakaru Gendai Mahou,</i> on sale
as part of Shueisha's Super Dash Paperbacks,

00:24:54.890 --> 00:25:24.330
As part of Shueisha's Super Dash Paperbacks,
Volume 6 now on sale!

00:24:58.010 --> 00:25:02.630
is currently up to vol. 6, <i>Firefox!</i>.

00:25:02.630 --> 00:25:04.480
You can watch the anime
every week,

00:25:04.480 --> 00:25:07.700
but if you haven't read
the novels yet,

00:25:07.700 --> 00:25:13.120
how about using our wonderful adventures
for summer reading this year?

00:25:13.120 --> 00:25:16.040
It'll complement the second
half of the show.

00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:18.890
Teacher, it's all text...

00:25:18.890 --> 00:25:21.950
Well, it's a novel.
What did you expect?

00:25:21.950 --> 00:25:24.180
Jeez, Koyomi.

00:25:24.180 --> 00:25:26.320
How about reading this, too?

00:25:24.870 --> 00:25:41.390
<i>Jump Comics</i> volume 1

00:25:24.870 --> 00:25:41.390
flying off shelves!

00:25:26.320 --> 00:25:27.560
Okay!

00:25:27.600 --> 00:25:31.150
It's the first volume from
Jump Comics, right?

00:25:31.150 --> 00:25:35.340
Miyashita Miki-san, who also
illustrates the novels,

00:25:35.340 --> 00:25:38.020
draws this comic, currently serialized
in<i> Jump Square.</i>

00:25:38.020 --> 00:25:41.760
And volume 1 is flying off
the shelves right now!

00:25:41.760 --> 00:25:46.310
Koyomi's gonna read all the novels
and comics this summer,

00:25:46.310 --> 00:25:52.360
and get about 256 times more
knowledgeable on Modern-Day Magic!

00:25:52.360 --> 00:25:54.680
That's some determination
you have there, Koyomi.

00:25:54.680 --> 00:25:57.760
You're going to read them all
and hand in a book report.

00:25:57.760 --> 00:25:59.290
What?!

00:25:59.290 --> 00:26:02.260
Save me...

00:26:02.260 --> 00:26:04.260
See you next week!
